%%%%** Section 3.3
\subsection{Voltage Levels and Rise Times:}
<*chn>
\begin{center}
   \includegraphics[height=2in]{usb_figs/00078.eps}   \\
(Figure 7-1, page 107)
\end{center}


%<s>\vspace{-2in}
<s>  \scalebox{.15}{  \includegraphics{usb_figs/00078.eps} }\\


<s>\end{slide}
<s>\begin{slide}


<*>
Driver Low, V{\sc ol},  must be $<$ 0.3v (1.5k$\Omega$ to 3.6V)

Driver High, V{\sc oh}, must be $>$ 2.8v (15k$\Omega$ to 0V)

Receiver High, V{\sc ih}, $>$ 2.0V must be detected as High

Receiver Low, V{\sc il}, $<$ 0.8V must be detected as Low

Worst case inputs: [-1.0V --- +4.6V]

90$\Omega$ characteristic impedance (high speed)

<s>\end{slide}
<s>\begin{slide}
%%%%** Section 3.4
\subsection{Differential Drive (``Gen-1'')}
<s> \scalebox{0.15}{
<chn>\scalebox{0.15}{
    \includegraphics{usb_figs/00079.eps}
   }

(Fig 7-2 page 108)

Single duplex: used one direction at a time.

D+ and D- usually signal by their {\it difference}

This eliminates common mode noise

{\tt OE} enables the output drivers.

<s>\end{slide}
<s>\begin{slide}
%%%%** Section 3.5
\subsection{Signaling Levels (high speed)}

Differential ``1'':  (D+ $-$ D-) $>$ 200mV

Differential ``0'':  (D- $-$ D+) $>$ 200mV

Idle: Differential ``1''

Start of Packet (SOP):  Idle $\to$ Differential ``0''

(``J" and ``K" states (!))

Reset:   D+ and D- $<$ 0.8V for $>=$ 10 ms.

<s>\end{slide}
<s>\begin{slide}
%%%%** Section 4
\section{Modulation and Channel Coding}
%%%%** Section 4.1
\subsection{NRZI}

Non Return to Zero:

Logic zero is sent by toggling

Logic one is sent by not toggling

{\tt Data} $\to$ {\tt NRZI Signal }

{\tt
00000000 $\to$  01010101

11111111 $\to$  11111111
}

<s>\end{slide}
<s>\begin{slide}
%%%%** Section 4.2
\subsection{Bit Stuffing}

Packets don't have as many start and stop bits as RS-232

Receiver needs to see 1$\to$0 or 0$\to$1 transitions at
least every seven bits.

Bit-stuffing inserts a zero whenever there are 6 ones
in a row.

{\tt
11111111 $\to$  111111011
}

Now the receiver sees at least a few transitions for {\it any}
data stream and so it can keep its clock phase locked.

Receiver hardware automatically removes stuffed bits.

<s>\end{slide}
<s>\begin{slide}
%%%%** Section 4.3
\subsection{Update: USB 2.0 }

Released April 2000.

Logically the same as 1.1, backwards compatible.

Provides additional speed mode:  {\bf Hi-Speed}  480 Mbit/s

Caution: if a device is labeled ``Full Speed USB 2.0" you are really getting USB 1.1 (!)

Only ``High Speed" or ``480 Mbit/s" is a ``real" USB 2.0 device.

<s>\end{slide}
<s>\begin{slide}

%%%%** Section 5
\section{Modern USB (2008--present)}
\begin{center}
{\bf WARNING: AI Generated material for rest of deck!!\\
